{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered.</b> This Name is the attribute of justice, and it was transformed to the attribute of mercy through the prayer of the righteous; and the wickedness of the wicked transforms the attribute of mercy to the attribute of justice, as it says ״וַיַּרְא יְהוָה כִּי רַבָּה רָעַת הָאָדָם,״ and ״וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶמְחֶה״ (Genesis 6) — and that is the Name of the attribute of mercy:" "<b>And Elohim remembered Noah, etc.</b> What did He remember for the beasts? Merit — that they did not corrupt their way beforehand and that they did not mate in the ark." "<b>And Elohim passed a wind.</b> A spirit of consolation and rest passed before Him." "<b>Over the earth.</b> Over the affairs of the earth." "<b>And the waters subsided.</b> As in ״כְּשֹׁךְ חֲמַת הַמֶּלֶךְ״ (Esther 2) — a term of calming anger."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:56.672191088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}